"""
motu424-probe-gui - MOTU PCI-324 / PCI-424 / PCIe-424 Card Probe & BAR Inspector

A standalone GTK4 engineering GUI for detecting MOTU PCI audio cards, inspecting
PCI BAR mappings (Window A 8MB, Window B 4MB audio aperture, I/O-port bridge),
and dumping live hardware registers and memory for reverse-engineering.

Features:
  - PCI device scanner for Mark of the Unicorn cards (vendor 0x137A)
  - Full BAR breakdown and classification against the RE hardware model
  - Interactive memory/register hex viewer with offset & length targeting
  - Presets for Bank 0/1 control words, aperture base, and BAR heads
  - Live memory diff mode (compare idle vs streaming states)
  - Driver unbind/bind helper (raw register probing requires unbound driver)
  - Simulated demo mode (--demo) for testing without physical hardware
  - Export to clipboard (hex dump or C array) and file saving

Usage:
  ./tools/motu424-probe-gui            # Auto-detect hardware
  ./tools/motu424-probe-gui --demo     # Run with simulated PCIe-424 card
  ./tools/motu424-probe-gui 0000:02:00.0 # Target specific PCI device
"""

