            "### 1. Dual-Window MMIO Architecture\n"
            "The vendor Windows driver (`MOTUAW.sys`) models the PCI-424 hardware via two MMIO windows:\n"
            "  - **Window A (8 MB, dev-ext +0x7c):** Used for bulk 8-dword block writes (`WriteBlock8` at VA 0x291a0).\n"
            "  - **Window B (4 MB, dev-ext +0x78):** The audio streaming aperture ring buffer and bank register file.\n"
            "  - **I/O-Port Bridge (dev-ext +0x80):** Status at `+0x0` (bit 1 = ready/pending), strobe strobe at `+0x4`.\n\n"
            "### 2. The Gaps Gating Audio Streaming\n"
            "The driver implements the reverse-engineered hardware model, but audio streaming is refused until\n"
            "two runtime addresses are supplied:\n"
            "  1. `motu424.audio_base=0x...`: Window B card offset of the audio register block\n"
            "     (stream enable +0x54, rate family +0x60, position counter +0x2c).\n"
            "  2. `motu424.ack_addr=0x...`: Card address where writing `0x10` clears the hardware interrupt.\n\n"
            "### 3. Procedure to Discover Runtime Addresses\n"
            "  1. **Idle Dump:** Dump Window B registers while the card is idle.\n"
            "  2. **Streaming Dump:** Start playback in Windows (via VM/dual-boot) or test stream, and dump Window B again.\n"
            "  3. **Diff:** The registers that toggle or increment (sample counter at `audio_base + 0x2c`) reveal the addresses.\n"
            "  4. **Inject:** Load module with `sudo insmod kernel/motu424.ko audio_base=0x... ack_addr=0x...`\n\n"
            "### 4. CLI Helper\n"
            "You can also run the userspace CLI dumper directly:\n"
            "  `sudo ./tools/motu424-probe`\n"
            "  `sudo ./tools/motu424-probe 0000:02:00.0 0xc0000 0x400`\n"
        )

        lbl = Gtk.Label()
        lbl.set_xalign(0.0)
        lbl.set_selectable(True)
        lbl.set_wrap(True)
        lbl.set_text(guide_text)
        box.append(lbl)

